    credentials and re-check every redirect against the rules
  * TUI, desktop and GUI plugins: plugin themes and CodeBlock
    registries; mobile composer dock; scroll-on-send setting;
    prompt history kept to 200 entries; many crash and focus
    fixes
  * Many more fixes and improvements
- Lockstep to the opentui 0.8.3 runtime: the tag pins @opentui/*
  0.8.1 but Factory ships only 0.8.3, so the tree is rebased onto
  0.8.3 through upstream's own script/upgrade-opentui.ts before
  the install and %prep checks that pin; the 0.8.3 highlight
  queries are byte-identical to 0.8.0's, so the packaged
  tree-sitter modules and versions are unchanged
- Refresh the pty helper sources: packages/process-daemon 0.4.0
  to 0.5.0 (new Source20; ghostty-revision unchanged, so
  Source22 is untouched) with its locked cargo closure
  re-vendored (new vendor.tar.zst, file set identical); the npm
  @opencode/pty in the tree stays 0.4.0
- Retrace the vendor keep list (350 of 1846 store entries): the
  closure moves for effect 4.0.6 to 4.1.0 (new
  @effect/sql-sqlite-bun) and @opentui 0.8.0 to 0.8.3 with
  their re-resolved entries
- Legal review re-derived for the new tree: 347 packages, same
  10-licence set (MIT 190, Apache-2.0 67, ISC 65, rest as
  before) except the two @opentui/core-linux-* 0.8.3 entries now
  declaring MIT AND LGPL-2.1-or-later (was MIT; opentui 0.8.3
  decodes video via FFmpeg built from source in its own
  package, whose License tag carries the grant). Their prebuilt
  .so files are deleted from the tree and the runtime loads the
  opentui package's build instead, so no copyleft ships here;
  no proprietary packages - the @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk
  0.3.301 stays externalized (see below), and the retraced tree
  still drops its store entry with zero SDK bytes in the
  tarball
- Build web-tree-sitter's tree-sitter.wasm from source instead of
  shipping the npm prebuilt: emcc compiles the tree-sitter 0.25.10
  sources (new Source30) to the MAIN_MODULE the grammar side
  modules link against (EXPORT_ALL keeps env.__stack_pointer
  for emscripten 6), and bun rebundles the TS bindings the way
  upstream's script/build.js does; glue and wasm come from the
  same build.
  The npm prebuilts leave the vendor tarball at tarball time, the
  Source-Binary-Exception goes away with them, and %check (which
  loads every system grammar through this runtime) is the
  acceptance test; new BuildRequires: emscripten >= 6.0.3
- All five patches apply clean against 2.2.6 (with offsets
  only); fff 0.10.5, bun-pty 0.4.11, photon-node 0.3.4 and
  parcel 2.5.1 are unchanged, so the %prep pin checks pass
  unmodified; bun 1.4.4 now matches the tag's pin, so Patch0 is
  an inert guard for the next skew; no new runtime
  dependencies

