    pruning), the cargo closure loses its Windows-only import
    libs and wasm-only artifacts (with .cargo-checksum.json
    repair per crate), and Ghostty's zig-pkg/ loses its test/
    and examples/ dirs; %check proves the payload carries the
    from-source sha256 and the npm binaries are gone
  * OPENCODE_ZIG_CPU=baseline matches upstream's release builds;
    Ghostty ab0b9da9 ships with .git plus a pre-fetched zig-pkg/
    so the whole helper build runs with no network
  * New BuildRequires: cargo-packaging, git-core and zig 0.16.0;
    new Provides: bundled(opencode-pty); legal review extended
    for the helper's closure, still no copyleft and no
    proprietary code

